    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0788" n="772" xml:id="pg772"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.24/12–149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Peru </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-12-08T17:00:00-05:00">December 8, 1949—5
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>423. Peru Amb visited Dept Fri<anchor n="1" xml:id="d474-f1"/> offering token
                    payt unspecified quantity <hi rendition="#italic">soles</hi> as prelude to
                    formal L–L sett arrangement for later negot. Conversion rate not
                        mentioned.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d474-f2"/> (Embtel 699 Dec 1) Amb informed
                    offer appreciated but Dept unable consider any <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >soles</hi> payt not covered by formal sett specifying over-all terms of
                    payt and exch rate. No conclusion reached. Dept agreed to furnish Amb this week
                    draft sett formula which it believes would be acceptable to Dept. Further info
                        airmail.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d474-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d474-f1" n="1" xml:id="d474-f1-content">
                <p>December 2, 1049.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d474-f2" n="2" xml:id="d474-f2-content">
                <p>On November 14, the Government of Peru had abolished the official exchange rate
                    of 6.50 <hi rendition="#italic">soles</hi> to the dollar, thus ending the dual
                    system of official and free rates for the <hi rendition="#italic">sol.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d474-f3" n="3" xml:id="d474-f3-content">
                <p>See instruction No. 310, December 28, to Lima, <ref target="#pg775">p.
                    775</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
